class:: GendyS709
summary:: Internal periodic modulation of stochastic waveform motion
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>GENDY
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Guides/Stochastica-GENDY, Classes/Gendy77, Classes/Gendy91, Classes/GendyField, Classes/GendyPerc, Classes/GendyInterp, Classes/GendyDiffusion, Classes/GendyCoupled

description::
strong::Historically informed adaptation.::

Adds sine or sawtooth parameter modulation to a first-order remembered waveform. Luque (2006), printed p. 31, describes such modulation in S.709 (1994), link::https://sergioluque.com/stochastics::. Hoffmann's 2023 dictionary distinguishes its direct breakpoint drive from Gendy3's intermediary walks: link::https://www.iannis-xenakis.org/en/stochastic-synthesis/::.

The original routing, depths and exact parameter values are not sufficiently specified by these sources. This class uses one bipolar internal modulator m and positive exponential factors 2.pow(depth*m) for amplitude mobility, duration mobility and a common frequency shift. Those routes are Stochastica choices, not a bit-exact S.709 reconstruction. The phase runs at audio rate; walk controls are sampled at cycle boundaries. All depths zero exactly matches Gendy77 with shape controls at one.

The oscillator remembers one amplitude and one incoming duration per point. Updates occur once per waveform cycle, in index order; a newly evolved first point connects from the actual previous cycle endpoint. Durations are fractional sample counts with carried remainder and a one-sample minimum. High settings therefore saturate the achievable frequency range. There is no antialiasing, automatic DC removal or loudness normalization. Start quietly; the examples use LeakDC and a short fade.

Construction/reset starts amplitudes at zero and durations at the midpoint of their bounds. Motion builds an audible waveform over the first cycles; zero amplitude mobility at construction stays silent. A later freeze retains the evolved waveform. Reset can deliberately interrupt continuity. Invalid selectors and numeric controls are conditioned to documented finite bounds; non-finite frequencies use 100/1000 Hz defaults.

Like vanilla link::Classes/Gendy1:: with external periodic control signals, this can move between restrained and rough motion. GendyS709 packages a resettable internal phase and explicit coupled modulation routes.

image::gendy-gendys709.png::


classmethods::
method:: ar
argument:: ampDist
Amplitude innovation law: 0 uniform, 1 truncated Cauchy, 2 truncated logistic, 3 truncated hyperbolic secant, 4 arcsine, 5 mapped truncated exponential. Integer clipped to 0..5; see the GENDY guide for quantiles. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durDist
Duration innovation law, using the same IDs as ampDist. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: minFreq
Lower frequency bound in Hz, giving the longest segment fs/(numPoints*minFreq). Bounds are sorted and clipped to 0.001..fs/numPoints. Sampled at cycle entry; this is not fixed-pitch normalization.
argument:: maxFreq
Upper frequency bound in Hz, giving the shortest segment fs/(numPoints*maxFreq). Equal frequency bounds fix segment duration. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: ampStep
Amplitude step as a fraction of the full interval width 2, clipped to 0..1. Once sampled, zero freezes further amplitude updates. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durStep
Duration step as a fraction of the current duration interval width, clipped to 0..1. Zero freezes duration motion with fixed frequency bounds. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: modFreq
Internal modulator frequency in Hz, clipped to 0..fs/2 and read each audio sample. Zero holds its phase. Reset restores phase zero.
argument:: modShape
0 sine or 1 ascending bipolar saw; clipped/truncated. Both use the same internal phase. At phase zero the sine is zero and the saw is -1. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: ampStepDepth
0..4 octaves of amplitude-mobility modulation. Effective ampStep = base*2.pow(depth*m), then clipped to 0..1. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: durStepDepth
0..4 octaves of duration-mobility modulation using the same bipolar m. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: freqRangeDepth
0..4 octaves of common frequency-bound motion, preserving their ratio until safety clipping. Sampled at cycle entry.
argument:: numPoints
Construction-time number of remembered breakpoints, clipped to 2..64 and truncated to an integer. Recreate the Synth to change it.
argument:: reset
Nonpositive-to-positive edge rewinds the original local seed, all point states and scheduler state. The reset sample equals the first sample of a fresh instance; a held positive value does not keep resetting. Audio-rate reset is supported.
argument:: seed
Construction-time local PCG32 seed. Nonzero seeds repeat for identical inputs and rate. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth RNG once; reset reuses it. Cross-platform last-bit differences are possible.
returns::
One audio-rate waveform, bounded to -1..1 before external scaling. No control-rate constructor is provided.

examples::
subsection:: Minimal example
code::
(
{ LeakDC.ar(GendyS709.ar(seed: 709)) ! 2 * 0.07 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Slow changes in stochastic activity
A four-second sine changes both mobility and register, making the modulation audible without requiring a long wait.
code::
(
{
    var x = GendyS709.ar(minFreq: 100, maxFreq: 300, ampStep: 0.04, durStep: 0.025,
        modFreq: 0.25, ampStepDepth: 2, durStepDepth: 2, freqRangeDepth: 0.5, seed: 42);
    LeakDC.ar(x) ! 2 * 0.07 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
